Columns: inputs of p1 p2 p3. Cell: decision values reachable over all
delivery orders; 0/1 = bivalent; ! = two processes can decide differently;
~ = some order leaves a live process undecided; - = nobody ever decides.

Protocol W3: wait for all three values, decide the majority
                 000    001    010    011    100    101    110    111   
  nobody silent  0      0      0      1      0      1      1      1     
  p1 silent      -      -      -      -      -      -      -      -     
  p2 silent      -      -      -      -      -      -      -      -     
  p3 silent      -      -      -      -      -      -      -      -     
  (5808 complete delivery orders explored)

Protocol W2: wait for own value + one more, decide (tie -> 0)
                 000    001    010    011    100    101    110    111   
  nobody silent  0      0      0      0/1!   0      0/1!   0/1!   1     
  p1 silent      0      0      0      1      0      0      0      1     
  p2 silent      0      0      0      0      0      1      0      1     
  p3 silent      0      0      0      0      0      0      1      1     
  (432 complete delivery orders explored)

Chain 000 -> 100 -> 110 -> 111 for W3, nobody silent:
  000 : 0
  100 : 0
  110 : 1
  111 : 1
  100 and 110 differ only in p2's input but decide differently.
  With p2 silent: 100 -> -, 110 -> - (W3 waits forever)
  W2 with p2 silent: 100 -> 0, 110 -> 0 (same, as it must be)
